<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<%- include('partials/head', {title, meta, og, twitter, schema, canonical, trackingId}) %>
<body>

<div id="dw-preloader">
  <div class="dw-preloader-bar"></div>
</div>

<%- include('partials/header') %>

<section class="inner-page-hero">
  <div class="dw-container">
    <div class="breadcrumb-dw">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span class="breadcrumb-sep">/</span>
      <span>FAQ</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="inner-page-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
    <p class="inner-page-sub">
      Everything you need to know about working with Dadword IT.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="faq-section">
  <div class="dw-container">
    <div class="faq-grid">

      <div class="faq-col">
        <div class="faq-item" data-faq>
          <button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="true">
            What services do you offer?
            <span class="faq-icon"><%- include('partials/icon', { name: 'plus' }) %></span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>We specialise in custom web portals, Shopify app development, SaaS product builds, and AI-enhanced delivery pipelines. This covers everything from architecture and backend APIs to frontend interfaces and long-term support.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" data-faq>
          <button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">
            How long does a typical project take?
            <span class="faq-icon"><%- include('partials/icon', { name: 'plus' }) %></span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>A focused MVP typically ships in 6 to 12 weeks. Larger platforms or multi-phase SaaS products can run 3 to 6 months. We provide a detailed timeline after understanding your scope and priorities in the discovery call.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" data-faq>
          <button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">
            Do you take on small projects or only large builds?
            <span class="faq-icon"><%- include('partials/icon', { name: 'plus' }) %></span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>We work best with projects that have a clear problem and a growth ambition behind them, small or large. We do not take on simple template tweaks, but a focused feature build for a growing product is absolutely within scope.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" data-faq>
          <button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">
            Do you offer post-launch support and maintenance?
            <span class="faq-icon"><%- include('partials/icon', { name: 'plus' }) %></span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Yes. We offer retainer-based support plans that cover bug fixes, security patches, performance monitoring, and iterative feature development. Many of our clients stay with us long after launch.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-col">
        <div class="faq-item" data-faq>
          <button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">
            Do you use templates or build everything custom?
            <span class="faq-icon"><%- include('partials/icon', { name: 'plus' }) %></span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Everything we ship is purpose-built for your product. We do not resell or reskin generic templates. Custom architecture means your codebase is yours to own, extend, and scale without lock-in.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" data-faq>
          <button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">
            Will the product be mobile-responsive?
            <span class="faq-icon"><%- include('partials/icon', { name: 'plus' }) %></span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Always. Every interface we design is fully responsive across phones, tablets, and desktops. Mobile performance is treated as a first-class requirement, not an afterthought.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" data-faq>
          <button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">
            What is "AI-Enhanced Development"?
            <span class="faq-icon"><%- include('partials/icon', { name: 'plus' }) %></span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>We use AI-assisted coding tools (including Cursor and Claude) as part of our engineering workflow. This lets our senior engineers ship faster without cutting corners on quality, which means shorter timelines and lower costs for you.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" data-faq>
          <button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">
            How do I get started?
            <span class="faq-icon"><%- include('partials/icon', { name: 'plus' }) %></span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Book a free 30-minute discovery call via our <a href="/lets-talk">Let's Talk</a> page. We will ask about your goals, timeline, and budget, and give you honest feedback on fit and approach before any commitment.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="faq-cta">
      <p>Still have questions?</p>
      <a href="/contact-us" class="dw-btn-outline">Drop us a message</a>
      <a href="/lets-talk" class="dw-btn-primary">Book a free call</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('partials/footer', { recent_blogs: recent_blogs }) %>
<script src="/js/dadword.js" defer></script>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-faq]').forEach(item => {
    const btn = item.querySelector('.faq-q');
    const ans = item.querySelector('.faq-a');
    const isOpen = btn.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
    if (isOpen) item.classList.add('open');
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const opening = !item.classList.contains('open');
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-faq]').forEach(f => {
        f.classList.remove('open');
        f.querySelector('.faq-q').setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
      });
      if (opening) {
        item.classList.add('open');
        btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
      }
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
.inner-page-hero {
  padding-top: 140px;
  padding-bottom: 60px;
}
.inner-page-title {
  font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  line-height: 1.2;
  margin: 12px 0 16px;
}
.inner-page-sub {
  font-size: 1.05rem;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  max-width: 560px;
}

.faq-section { padding-bottom: 100px; }

.faq-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  gap: 0 48px;
  margin-bottom: 60px;
}
@media (max-width: 768px) { .faq-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

.faq-col { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0; }

.faq-item {
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
}
.faq-item:first-child { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }

.faq-q {
  width: 100%;
  background: none;
  border: none;
  padding: 20px 0;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 16px;
  text-align: left;
  font-size: .95rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--text-primary);
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: color .2s;
}
.faq-q:hover { color: var(--accent); }
.faq-icon {
  width: 28px;
  height: 28px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  flex-shrink: 0;
  font-size: .65rem;
  color: var(--text-faint);
  transition: all .25s;
}
.faq-item.open .faq-q { color: var(--accent); }
.faq-item.open .faq-icon {
  background: var(--accent);
  border-color: var(--accent);
  color: #fff;
  rotate: 45deg;
}

.faq-a {
  max-height: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
  transition: max-height .35s ease, padding .35s ease;
}
.faq-a p {
  padding-bottom: 20px;
  font-size: .88rem;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  line-height: 1.75;
  margin: 0;
}
.faq-a p a { color: var(--accent); }
.faq-item.open .faq-a { max-height: 300px; }

.faq-cta {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 16px;
  padding: 32px 36px;
  background: var(--surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 16px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}
.faq-cta p {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: .9rem;
  flex: 1;
  min-width: 140px;
}
</style>

</body>
</html>
